   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize the East Northport Fire Department to receive retroactive\nreal property tax exempt status",
    "basePrintNo": "S3735",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3735-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S3735\n\nSPONSOR: FLANAGAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to authorize the East Northport Fire Department\nto receive retroactive real property tax exempt status\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo allow a retroactive application for real property tax exemption for\nthe East Northport Fire Department located in Suffolk County.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1-Would authorize the assessor of Suffolk County to accept from\nthe East Northport Fire Department (ENFD) an application for exemption\nfrom real property taxes with respect to subdivision 2 of section 464 of\nthe real property tax law. If satisfied that the ENFD would otherwise be\nentitled to such exemption, the assessor upon approval by the Suffolk\nCounty Legislature, may, in its sole discretion, provide for the refund\nof those taxes paid and cancel those taxes, fines, penalties, liens, or\ninterest remaining unpaid.\n\nSection 2-Provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe East Northport Fire Department was founded in 1908 for the purpose\nof organizing a local fire department that would help protect the citi-\nzens of the community. Throughout that time, the members of the ENFD\nhave saved countless lives and have answered the call to action thou-\nsands of times, putting their lives at risk in the service of others.\nThis legislation would provide the ENFD with the opportunity to acquire\nmuch-deserved relief in the realm of property taxes.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019: New Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
