    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S3735B\n\nSPONSOR: FLANAGAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act in relation to authorizing the East Northport\nFire District to file an application for a real property tax exemption\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo allow a retroactive application for real property tax exemption for\nthe East Northport Fire District located in Suffolk County.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1-Would authorize the assessor of the Town of Huntington to\naccept from the East Northport Fire District (ENFD) an application for\nexemption from real property taxes with respect section 406 of the real\nproperty tax law. If satisfied that the ENFD would otherwise be entitled\nto such exemption, the assessor upon approval by the Huntington Town\nBoard, may, in its sole discretion, provide for the refund of those\ntaxes paid and cancel those taxes, fines, penalties, liens, or interest\nremaining unpaid.\n\nSection 2-Provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe East Northport Fire District was founded in 1908 for the purpose of\norganizing a local fire department that would help protect the citizens\nof the community. Throughout that time, the members of the ENFD have\nsaved countless lives and have answered the call to action thousands of\ntimes, putting their lives at risk in the service of others. This legis-\nlation would provide the ENFD with the opportunity to acquire much-de-\nserved relief in the realm of property taxes.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2019: New Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately\n",
